```

**Step 2:** Run: `cargo test -p lattice-ui-tui --lib file_tree 2>&1 | tail -15`

Expected: compile error — `open` takes 1 arg, not 2.

**Step 3:** Update `FileTreeBuffer` and `render_to_buffer`:

- Add `pub nerd_fonts: bool` field to `FileTreeBuffer`
- Change `open(root: impl Into<PathBuf>)` → `open(root: impl Into<PathBuf>, nerd_fonts: bool)`, pass to render, store on struct
- Change `toggle_at` to call `render_to_buffer(&self.entries, self.nerd_fonts)`
- Change `render_to_buffer(entries: &[FileTreeEntry])` → `render_to_buffer(entries: &[FileTreeEntry], nerd_fonts: bool)`, add icon embedding:

```rust
fn render_to_buffer(entries: &[FileTreeEntry], nerd_fonts: bool) -> Buffer {
    use crate::icons::icon_for_entry;
    use crate::theme::Theme;
    let theme = Theme::default();
    let mut text = String::new();
    for (i, entry) in entries.iter().enumerate() {
        let indent = "  ".repeat(entry.depth as usize);
        let marker = match entry.kind {
            FileTreeEntryKind::Directory { expanded: true }  => "▾ ",
            FileTreeEntryKind::Directory { expanded: false } => "▸ ",
            FileTreeEntryKind::File                          => "  ",
        };
        let is_dir = matches!(entry.kind, FileTreeEntryKind::Directory { .. });
        let (icon, _style) = icon_for_entry(&entry.path, is_dir, nerd_fonts, &theme);
        let name = if entry.depth == 0 {
            entry.path.display().to_string()
        } else {
            entry.path.file_name()
                .map(|s| s.to_string_lossy().into_owned())
                .unwrap_or_default()
        };
        text.push_str(&indent);
        text.push_str(marker);
        text.push_str(icon);
        text.push_str(&name);
        if i + 1 < entries.len() {
            text.push('\n');
        }
    }
    let mut buffer = Buffer::empty();
    if !text.is_empty() {
        let _ = buffer.apply_edit(&Edit::insert(Position::ZERO, text));
    }
    buffer
}
```

- Fix all existing tests to pass `false` as the `nerd_fonts` arg. The existing test `render_uses_indentation_and_marker` checks `body.lines().nth(1).unwrap().starts_with("    ")` — with `nerd_fonts=false` the icon is `""` (empty) so 4 spaces of indent (2 indent + 2 marker spaces) still holds.

**Step 4:** Fix the one call site in `app.rs` line 12203:
```rust
